WEBVTT

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:03.960
Digital footprints are observable traces created through active sharing,

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:08.220
passive collection, public records, technical infrastructure, and third-party references.

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:11.340
They can be personal, professional, organizational, or technical,

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:12.580
and they change over time.

00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:16.790
Active footprints include posts, profiles, documents, and code intentionally published.

00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:21.160
Passive footprints include logs, indexing, metadata, tracking, data-broker records,

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:22.910
and reported service exposure.

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:27.180
One item may be low risk while aggregation reveals sensitive relationships, routines,

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:28.140
or infrastructure.

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:32.925
Responsible analysis validates identity, origin, accuracy, timeliness, and context.

00:00:32.925 --> 00:00:36.570
It distinguishes ownership from association and current conditions from historical

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:37.055
records.

00:00:37.055 --> 00:00:41.090
Public availability never authorizes harassment, doxxing, impersonation,

00:00:41.090 --> 00:00:44.065
unauthorized access, or misuse of personal information.

00:00:44.065 --> 00:00:47.890
Risk reduction combines account security, privacy settings, careful publishing,

00:00:47.890 --> 00:00:52.330
metadata review, asset ownership, repository and service hygiene, employee awareness,

00:00:52.330 --> 00:00:55.340
and recurring monitoring for legitimate defensive purposes.

00:00:55.340 --> 00:00:58.490
The objective is intentional control, not total disappearance.

00:00:58.490 --> 00:01:02.890
A well-managed footprint supports useful public communication and accountable operations

00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:04.750
while limiting unnecessary detail.

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:09.200
Ethical analysis uses proportionality and evidence to reduce privacy and security risk

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:12.240
without exploiting the people represented by the data.
